# Changelog

## Adaptive Vehicle Intelligence Architecture Engineering Repository – Public (AER-PU)

---

## Purpose

The purpose of this document is to provide a structured and traceable record of significant changes made to the Adaptive Vehicle Intelligence Architecture Engineering Repository – Public (AER-PU).

The changelog preserves the historical evolution of the repository by documenting major milestones, approved modifications, governance updates, engineering publications, and repository improvements.

---

# Changelog Philosophy

Engineering knowledge evolves over time.

The purpose of the changelog is not simply to record that something changed, but to document the engineering significance of the change and preserve the history of repository evolution.

The changelog complements version control by recording meaningful engineering milestones rather than low-level file modifications.

---

# Scope

This changelog records:

- Repository governance updates
- Repository structure changes
- Publication of approved engineering documents
- Repository policy revisions
- Major engineering milestones
- Baseline releases
- Repository-wide improvements

The changelog does not record:

- Minor spelling corrections
- Formatting changes
- Temporary draft work
- Private engineering activities
- Experimental development

---

# Change Categories

Repository changes shall be classified into one or more of the following categories:

- Added
- Approved
- Changed
- Improved
- Deprecated
- Archived
- Removed
- Released

---

# Version History

## Version 1.0

Status: Active

Date: Repository Initialization

### Added

- Public Engineering Repository established.
- Repository description approved.
- README.md Baseline 1.0 published.
- GOVERNANCE.md Baseline 1.0 published.
- CONTRIBUTING.md Baseline 1.0 published.
- CHANGELOG.md Baseline 1.0 established.

### Approved

- Repository Governance Framework.
- Repository Contribution Framework.

### Released

- Repository Foundation Layer Version 1.0.

---

# Recording Policy

Every significant repository change shall include:

- Version
- Date
- Change Category
- Description
- Engineering significance (when applicable)

---

# Repository Milestones

The repository shall maintain a chronological record of significant engineering and governance milestones throughout the lifecycle of the AVIA project.

---

# Continuous Evolution

This changelog shall be updated whenever a significant repository milestone or approved engineering publication occurs.

Historical entries shall remain preserved to maintain repository traceability and engineering history.

